    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** (84.24) and **Yordan Alvarez** (82.60) serving as our undisputed anchors. **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Sugano (5.02 xERA), with his elevated xwOBA and +19% SP skill boost making him a primary source for HR and RBI upside. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in elite play; despite a minor park penalty, his elite contact metrics and favorable spot in the order against Taillon maximize our scoring ceiling. **Trea Turner** (70.50) also deserves special mention; his score is buoyed by a slow SP delivery from Irvin, J, which provides a high-leverage stolen base opportunity\u2014a critical metric for us given our emphasis on the scarcest category.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal range, where **Colt Keith** (48.79) was the primary candidate for a utility spot but ultimately failed to crack the top ten. While **Colt Keith** offers a slight boost in the stolen base department due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, his lower base projection relative to **Caleb Durbin**\u2014who offers better park factors\u2014kept him on the pine. We are also monitoring the volatility surrounding **Christian Yelich** (48.83); while he carries a respectable score, his efficiency is suppressed by facing an elite arm in Skenes and an elite catcher, making him a candidate for mid-game substitution if the Zebras gain a comfortable lead.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the strength of some opposing starters. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (70.99) projects well against Lauer, we have noted a significant platoon penalty (-15%) that makes him a high-variance play; however, his leadoff placement keeps his floor stable. **Lars Nootbaar** (58.44) and **Kyle Schwarber** (67.17) round out the lineup with strong plate appearances, though both managers should watch for weather shifts that could impact the high-scoring potential of their respective matchups. Players such as **Dillon Dingler**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** will remain on the bench to preserve our game caps, ensuring we only deploy the Zebras' most efficient assets during this critical stretch of the season.",
